# Nissan Sunny N13 five-door hatchback, 1986-1991.
#
# The fourth front-wheel-drive Sunny, the first with the rounded body that broke
# from the angular B310. The five-door hatchback is modelled; the three-door and
# the saloon differ at the rear side glass and tailgate and are not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Sunny
#
# Dimensions 4.150 x 1.670 x 1.395 m, wheelbase 2.430 m, from the English
# Wikipedia N13 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.884 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the N13 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, red, blue and silver. Weights white 3, red 3, blue 2,
# silver 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h for the 1.3, the volume UK engine. Comfort 80/300, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 80, the same as the Bluebird T12. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: October 1986 intro, retires staggered 2001-2004 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-sunny-n13.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-sunny-n13.dae (50 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-sunny-n13/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the bumper sections are simplified and the shoulders
# faceted. The photographs also show a straighter roof and body edge than the
# brief's description of a rounded body, and the model follows the photographs.
# At 128 px the hatch slope, the split grille and the horizontal rear lamps read
# correctly.

obj=citycar
name=NissanSunnyN13(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1986
intro_month=10
retire_year=2004
retire_month=6
speed=165
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=300

